# The repository's blobs are LF. Without this, a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true)
# rewrites text files to CRLF, which silently breaks any tool that parses raw source
# text rather than a normalized stream: Vite/vitest strip a `#!` hashbang only up to a
# bare "\n", so a CRLF shebang script (e.g. scripts/backfill-user-registry.mjs, imported
# by tests/backfill.test.ts) fails to load with a bare "Invalid or unexpected token".
# Pin LF on checkout everywhere so the working tree matches the blobs on every machine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Git hooks are pushed to the OS by their shebang line, and a CRLF shebang is a
# "bad interpreter" on every POSIX hook runner. Pin them explicitly rather than relying
# on the catch-all above: the failure is silent locally (Git for Windows tolerates CRLF)
# and total on a Mac or Linux checkout.
.githooks/* text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch their bytes.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.ico binary
